### 6. `bootstrap/falcon/001-link-app-to-env.http`

REST Client format (compatible with VS Code REST Client, IntelliJ HTTP Client). Variables
are resolved from the environment at runtime.

```http
### Login to obtain session cookie
POST {{FALCON_URL}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{TEST_USER}}",
  "password": "{{TEST_PASS}}"
}

### Create Development env for target-app-1 (idempotent via PUT)
PUT {{FALCON_URL}}/v1/apps/target-app-1/envs/Development
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: session={{SESSION_ID}}

{
  "host": "http://localhost:9000",
  "applicationId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000010"
}
```

Note: `{{SESSION_ID}}` is populated by the Runner from the Set-Cookie header of the login
response. When replaying manually, extract it with the `curl` snippet in the Manual Replay
Walkthrough section below.

