## Validation — What Success Looks Like

Run these commands after applying the seed. Each must return the expected result.

### eyas — user exists

```bash
psql "${EYAS_DB_URL}" -c \
  "SELECT 1 FROM users WHERE email='hawkscan-test@example.com';"
# Expected: 1 row
```

### eyas — org exists

```bash
psql "${EYAS_DB_URL}" -c \
  "SELECT 1 FROM organizations WHERE id='00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001';"
# Expected: 1 row
```

### eyas — membership exists

```bash
psql "${EYAS_DB_URL}" -c \
  "SELECT 1 FROM user_org_memberships
   WHERE user_id='00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002'
     AND org_id='00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001';"
# Expected: 1 row
```

### yarak — app exists

```bash
psql "${YARAK_DB_URL}" -c \
  "SELECT 1 FROM applications WHERE name='target-app-1';"
# Expected: 1 row
```

### falcon — env link exists

> Note: this curl requires the `SESSION` cookie set in Manual Replay Step 6. Run that step first.

```bash
# Requires the SESSION cookie obtained in Manual Replay Step 6
curl -s -H "Cookie: session=${SESSION}" "${FALCON_URL}/v1/apps/target-app-1/envs" | jq '.envs | length'
# Expected: ≥ 1
```

### Idempotency check

Re-run all seed steps. Then re-run the validation commands. Counts must not change.

### HawkScan authentication check

After bootstrap, with `.bootstrap-credentials.env` sourced, HawkScan configured against
the running falcon should authenticate successfully and find > 1 path during scan:

```bash
set -a; . ./.bootstrap-credentials.env; set +a
hawk scan   # or: hawkscan --config stackhawk.yml
```

A successful scan completes without a 401/403 and reports at least the `/login` route plus
one or more `/v1/*` routes.

